# Life and Limb (turn 1), Blood Moon (turn 3), then Arcane Adaptation naming Saproling (turn 5), all layer 4 (CR 613.1d): the
# board of blood-moon-life-and-limb-and-arcane-adaptation-making-a-saproling-depend-through-the-layer with Blood Moon and
# Adaptation the other way round. Judged on the whole game (CR 613.8a, 613.8c): Arcane Adaptation and Life and Limb depend
# on each other (a loop), Life and Limb also depends on Blood Moon, and Blood Moon on nothing. A loop is broken by timestamp
# order among its members, every other dependency kept (CR 613.8b; docs/rules-exceptions.md, RX-3): Adaptation and Blood
# Moon are ready, and Blood Moon is the earlier, so it applies first - Taiga is a Mountain and no Forest. Then Life and Limb
# applies to nothing until Adaptation makes the Elves a Saproling: Adaptation, then Life and Limb. The Elves are a 1/1 green
# Creature Land, Elf Druid Saproling Forest, tapping for {G} (Blood Moon applied before they were a land); Taiga is a plain
# Mountain, no creature, and taps for {R} alone.

